extraction_notes: "THE BOOK DECLARES THIS A COPY AND IT SHIPS WITHOUT `copy_of`. Printed 39 says the Side Kick RPA is \"basically the same as the Elite RPA Pilot O.C.C. described in the Rifts RPG, page 53... The stats are reprinted here for the reader''s convenience, along with modifications appropriate to the Quebec Military.\" A `copy_of` declaration cannot be written: this catalog holds no Elite RPA Pilot, and the nearest class, `robot-pilot`, is Rifts Ultimate Edition p.83-85 and is a DIFFERENT class - it requires P.S. 10, P.P. 12 and P.E. 12 where this one requires I.Q. 10 and P.P. 10. Declaring a copy of it would assert a match that does not hold and fail the regression sweep. So this is a standalone class carrying the Quebec printing, which is the side with the modifications anyway. NO SIDE KICK POWER ARMOR IN equipment_starting: the Side Kick is imported as a `vehicles` row (printed 92-94) and equipment_starting can only reference `gear` slugs, so the class ships without the one item its own book issues it. Recorded in restrictions where a player will see it. See BOOK-INGEST-AUDIT.md F3, and note this is the same cost the Noro Mystic Warrior paid. THIS ENTRY PRINTS NO O.C.C. BONUS LINE AT ALL - checked, not assumed; the `bonuses` block is absent because the book gives none, not because one was missed. Money: monthly salary 2,400 credits and one month''s pay to start."
---

## Lore

Side Kicks are a separate division within the Elite RPA. Their main type of
power armor is the Side Kick ' || char(8212) || ' a light, fast suit built to escort and support
Glitter Boys ' || char(8212) || ' but they can pilot SAMAS and other types of power armor and
armored vehicles just as well.

A Glitter Boy squad of 6-10 members is usually assigned two to four Side Kicks
and one Reload Team; an individual or pair of Taurus Glitter Boys is usually
assigned a Reload Team and a Side Kick of its own. Squads sent on covert or
intelligence-gathering missions may have anywhere from none to one Side Kick
each.

## GM Notes

Rank starts at Corporal.

Equipment available upon special assignment: other types of "non-Glitter Boy"
power armor, robot vehicles, tanks and APCs, hovercraft, sky cycle, jet pack,
transports and aircraft; any weapon types, extra ammunition, camera, disc
recorder, optical enhancement, and food rations for weeks, plus vehicle and
equipment repair. **All of it is allocated on the necessity of the assignment
and on availability** ' || char(8212) || ' and the book adds, dryly, that if the officer does not
like the character the availability of items may be extremely limited.

The soldier''s quarters is a dormitory shared with three others, each with a
private bedroom and study, CD stereo, television and VCD, mini-refrigerator,
desk, dresser and a comfortable bed.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'fq-side-kick-rpa');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'fq-side-kick-rpa';

